From 71a0893fe1af44c3e2eec247efe9b2a39ccf1627 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Paes <78096758+paesdan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:45:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] build: -Dweather_default, for a desk that asks the
 network nothing

The weather at the front door is on until a user turns it off: every half
hour the time zone city's latitude and longitude go to open-meteo.com. A
distribution that promises its machines contact nothing unasked needs it off
until the user turns it on, without relying on /etc/xdg/desk/shell.conf
being in place.

meson -Dweather_default=false builds DEsk with `weather` off where shell.conf
does not set it, and Shell Settings shows that default. The default build is
unchanged (on).

Signed-off-by: Daniel Paes <78096758+paesdan@users.noreply.github.com>
